WEBVTT

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.400
Eleven-eight.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.950
Game to Itsumo.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.120
Way to go, Hokuto!

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.650
Now it's two games each!

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.330
Amazing comeback, Hokuto-senpai!

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.100
Get that come-from-behind victory!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.430
Are you okay?

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.530
I'm fine.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.060
I'll win this.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.450
That's my Hokuto!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.230
Stop squeezing.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.120
Do your best, Hokuto-san.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.030
Thanks.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.230
<b>Scorching</b>

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.230
<b>Ping Pong Girls</b>

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.370
<i>I'll win, no matter what!</i>

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.940
I want to win.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.230
And take our first step
on the road to Nationals.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.400
I don't think that's happening.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.800
<b>Eighth Serve</b>

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.800
<b>Doubles</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.270
Don't worry, Yuragi-san.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.420
You still have the fifth game.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:48.960
Yeah.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.610
Refocus on the task at hand.
I know you can win this!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.570
Y-Yeah...

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.320
Zakuro's dropping pearls of wisdom.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.020
Never forget them,
even in death.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.710
I told you to stop that, Kururi!

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:03.920
Jeez!

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.780
You sure dragged this match out.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.850
It was just so adorable
how she came at me with all she had.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.250
Talk about a mean streak.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.590
She's ready to drop, you know?

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.550
Our training is leagues apart.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.940
We've lasted through
the most hellish regimens, haven't we?

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:23.710
Have.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:26.510
But she's still gonna try to win.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.440
I don't think that's happening.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.610
We're counting on you, Hokuto!

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:34.680
Win this!

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.720
She may not look it,
but her opponent's a tough one.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.780
They're tied at two games each,
but she hasn't even broken a sweat.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:46.100
Meanwhile, Hokuto's comeback
has taken a toll on a her.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.370
Stamina-wise, Yuragi has the upper hand.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.920
What?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.500
But they're about even in hits
from heated rallies!

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.760
She might be <i>forcing</i> Hokuto
into those long rallies.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.590
Her movements are unorthodox,
but they're highly efficient.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.950
In the fourth game,

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.550
her feet were moving
<i>before</i> Hokuto hit the ball.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:09.810
You mean she knew
where Hokuto-senpai would place her shots?

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.530
Maybe so.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.810
Mozuyama's starters
really can't be taken lightly.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.080
Racket Face Angle {tl}

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.080
Roll Direction {tr}

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.080
Wrist {b}

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.910
Wrist {t}

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.910
Muscular Tension {bl}

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.910
Elbow {b}

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.550
Love-one.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.140
Hokuto...

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:45.220
She really is predicting her moves!

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.650
Hokuto's serve is exceptionally accurate,

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:53.020
so its placement is easy to predict
if you figure out her tells.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.870
She'll have to work on that.

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.230
Why do you sound
like you've given up already?

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.730
But I haven't.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.610
Hokuto isn't a player to be taken lightly.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.250
<i>Sorry to say this,</i>

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.370
<i>but I can beat you with my eyes closed now.</i>

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.250
Payback's a bitch.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.380
Hokuto!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.210
Wow!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:19.840
A winner!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.430
You surprised me.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.570
I didn't think you had any tricks
left in your bag.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.230
This match isn't over yet.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:37.240
Right you are.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.230
Get ready, then,

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.190
for a long, long ride
on my pendulum!

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:46.290
Extended rallies are bad news for Hokuto.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.410
She has very little stamina left.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.740
Hokuto-san...

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.200
<i>I'll win, no matter what!</i>

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.660
<b>Suzumegahara 0 - 1 Mozuyama</b>

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.660
<b>Tenka Hanabi 2 - 3 Sasorida Sachiko</b>

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.620
<i>I have to win
and cancel out Hanabi's loss!</i>

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.790
I don't think that's happening.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.260
<i>It </i>is<i> happening!</i>

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:08.430
Hokuto!

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:15.320
Fourteen-twelve.

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:19.600
Game and match to Yuragi,
by a score of three games to two.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.170
Sorry. I went and lost.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:31.530
You were awesome, Hokuto.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.490
Let's work even harder,
so we both win next time.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:38.320
Yeah.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.880
Guess you won somehow,
though it was a close shave.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.360
Everything went according to—

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:55.600
Did you just stagger?
You did, didn't you?!

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.810
I did not.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:59.250
Well done, Yuragi-san.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.830
We're two up now.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.060
Let's keep this going.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:04.310
Y-Yes.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.520
You'd better go in with guns blazing.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.820
If you lose, practice will get even worse!

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:12.480
I know.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.240
At last, this time has come.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.740
Look at her!

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:24.920
Her eye!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.210
Really, is there any point to that?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.350
It's my thing.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.690
Whatever!

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.560
Just get out there and crush them!

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.190
Go, Kimiko!

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.850
Nom nom.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.270
More.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:53.070
Just go!

00:07:53.070 --> 00:08:01.750
<b>Tenka Hanabi                                 Sasorida Sachiko</b>

00:07:53.070 --> 00:08:01.750
<b>Itsumo Hokuto                                  Yuragi Yura</b>

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.580
We're two down, which means...

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.690
If we lose this next one,
we lose the whole match?

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:01.750
Watch your mouth!

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:04.030
I'm so sorry.

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.700
I'm so ashamed.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.250
Don't worry about it.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.330
Those were good games, you two.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:14.010
And you both found areas
to work on, so it's all good.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:19.100
I mean, our opponents are Mozuyama.
They're good enough to go to Nationals.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.310
Let's think of this
as a learning experience and take it easy.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.170
I can't take it easy.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:25.850
Never, ever.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.180
I want to win.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.280
I want us all to return victorious.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.960
And take our first step
on the road to Nationals.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:42.540
Hey, I have no intention of losing, either.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:47.760
We paid for the train fare here,
so we'd better win to make up for that.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.920
But you just said to take it easy!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:55.250
I mean, you two are facing
Mozuyama's captain and Futamaru-san.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:09:01.090
Even if we win, Mozuyama will take the day
if either of you lose,

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:03.140
so just relax and accept your fate.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.580
Wh-What the heck?!

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.010
I'll win, too!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:13.280
Can you really win?

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.820
I'm <i>winning</i>!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.150
And so will you, Koyori!

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.490
Y-Yeah.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.490
All right.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.640
Suzumegahara's comeback story begins now.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:27.080
Take it all in, first-years!

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.330
Yes!

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:31.530
It's time for the third match: doubles.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:34.050
Participants, please come to the table.

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:37.160
You got yelled at, huh?

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.930
Wasn't exactly what I was going for.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:46.030
I was just trying to tell them
to enjoy playing formidable opponents.

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:49.130
But aren't you the one most set on winning?

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:50.710
Of course.

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:53.780
I've never played table tennis
with a defeatist attitude.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.160
But enjoying ourselves takes priority.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.150
We haven't played doubles
in a while, after all.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:05.490
Oomune and Ushirode
versus Kanenashi and Hamu.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:07.210
Best-of-five games.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:10.490
First game. Ushirode to serve.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:12.090
Love-all!

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.760
One-love.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.720
Wow! They took the lead!

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.390
Are you okay?

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.540
That's some crazy power.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.690
I wonder what she eats to be like that.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:39.080
I <i>really</i> wonder what she eats.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:52.380
Two-love!

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:54.710
That's two points now.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.800
They're really good.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.580
Well, duh.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:02.250
They won all eight
of their matches last summer.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:04.180
All eight?

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.080
I was worried they'd be rusty,

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.640
but I guess that was
unnecessary concern on my part.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.230
A chopper and a smasher.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:17.380
I see.

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.320
So that's their combo.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:25.580
We saw loads of pairs
just like theirs at Nationals, didn't we?

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.840
I want meat buns now.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.180
Ain't got any.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:36.030
Buy me some, Kanenashi.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:40.530
Oh, fine.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:42.970
On our way home, then,

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.760
to celebrate our victory!

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.570
Nine-eight.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:05.490
Don't worry about it.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.450
Sorry.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:09.810
The momentum's changed hands
in the second game.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:12.660
Why aren't things going as smoothly
as in the first?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.130
It's the same as my match.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:18.590
The captain defends,
and Thong-senpai attacks.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.220
As ideal as that one-two punch is,
it's just as predictable.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:26.390
With the first game, the opponents
got a good grasp on their play style.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:30.310
I was wondering how they could play doubles
with their height difference,

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.060
but they know exactly how the other moves.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.980
And those two are forcing Thong-senpai
to play defense.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.320
Eight-ten.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.410
Eight-eleven.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.820
Game to Kanenashi and Hamu.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.460
The score is one game each.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:51.190
Munemune-senpai has a lethal smash,

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.540
but she makes errors
when she's on the back foot.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:57.290
<i>Even so, something's off with her today.</i>

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:00.710
Sorry.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.800
Don't worry about it.
There's still a long way to go.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.510
Looking good, girls.

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:07.720
All that practice is paying off.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:11.520
We owe it all to your coaching.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:15.720
Oh? Not often we hear you thank the seniors.

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:19.180
What? I'm always thankful to them!

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:23.110
You've pulled it back to one-all now,
but stay on your toes.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:25.080
Focus right until the end.

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:27.570
You got it.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.680
Nom! Nom!

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:31.540
You're making a real mess.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:37.000
<i>Zakuro's leading the juniors perfectly.</i>

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:41.250
<i>She's so dignified, so dependable.</i>

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:45.830
<i>This is how a true leader should look!</i>

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Suzumegahara          Mozuyama

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Tenka Hanabi                  Sasorida Sachiko

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Itsumo Hokuto                  Yuragi Yura

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Ushirode Kiruka
Munemune

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Kanenashi Mayuu
Hamu Kimiko

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Kamiya Agari                Zashikiwarashi Zakuro

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.640
Tsumujikaze Koyori                Futamaru Kururi

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:55.890
<i>Practice match or not,
I can't let Zakuro taste defeat.</i>

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.610
<i>I'm going to beat her to death.</i>

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.110
Why do you play
the life-or-death game of table tennis?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.990
I play for her!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:12.010
I can offer up all I have for Zakuro!

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:14.740
I'm prepared to die!

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:21.740
Now, it's time for the third game.

00:14:21.740 --> 00:14:24.300
Break a leg, Captain!

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.470
It's all on you.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.830
You can win this!

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.700
Take them out!

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.390
Thanks.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.610
Shall we go, Munemune?

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:39.350
Love-all.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.550
Her smashes can't break through anymore.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.950
No wonder they went to Nationals.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.950
<i>You're a good pair.</i>

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:12.640
<i>But we're not frail enough to turn tail
from something like this!</i>

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:21.570
<i>Not after we endured
that training from hell.</i>

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:31.660
Love-two.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.530
Nice.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.710
You, too.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:42.710
<i>I've got a long reach, and Kimiko's
as lovable and light-footed as a hamster.</i>

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.420
<i>We are a wall.</i>

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:53.590
<i>A perfect, immovable object
that stands between you and victory!</i>

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:05.750
They're returning Munemune-senpai's smashes
and the captain's chops.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.770
They're a well-balanced pair.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:09.150
That said...

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.030
Munemune.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.460
They're coming at me.

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:22.000
Yeah.

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:25.960
Sorry I'm holding you down on your return.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.360
You don't have to worry about that.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:32.010
But your play is kinda boring right now.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:35.590
You're worried about my ankle, aren't you?

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.660
That's why you can't focus on your game.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:46.650
Don't pay my ankle any mind. It'll be fine.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:47.560
But...

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:49.940
Remember what I said?

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:53.500
If I'm with you, no matter who I'm facing
or what shape I'm in,

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.070
I'll never lose.

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.620
Y-You're overrating me.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.350
But I mean it.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:04.730
If I'm with you, I'll never lose.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:09.210
Doesn't matter if I'm up against Mozuyama
or any other pair in the nation.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:15.210
We decided to become
number one together, didn't we?

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:20.810
Please get in position, Suzumegahara.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:22.240
Coming.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.290
Sorry about that.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:25.980
Let's go.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.910
My dream is to win Nationals
and become number one!

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.660
M-Me, too!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:43.180
My goal is to win Nationals, too!

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.290
I want to be number one, too!

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:51.200
<i>But neither of us...</i>

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.170
<i>...was good enough.</i>

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.330
<i>I have an aggressive,
error-prone play style,</i>

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.140
<i>and Kiruka lacks that killer shot.</i>

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:02.080
<i>Forget Nationals,</i>

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.140
<i>we couldn't even be top dog
on our own team.</i>

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.720
<i>But that's when we realized.</i>

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:11.780
<i>Together...</i>

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:14.480
<i>Together...</i>

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.690
<i>We can make up for what the other lacks.</i>

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:19.660
<i>Together, we're invincible!</i>

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:26.730
<i>So we decided to aim
for number one together.</i>

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:40.220
Are you sure you're all right?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:41.800
Wanna lick and see?

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.750
I keep telling you, I don't.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:55.980
Nom!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:56.940
Boring!

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:01.360
Two-one.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:03.230
Nailed it!

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.030
Beam.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:08.210
Kiruka.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.810
It's been a while. Bring it out.

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:15.670
Yeesh. You just won't let me stay bored.

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:18.890
It's not exactly my strong suit, you know.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.010
<i>Their aura suddenly changed.</i>

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.850
<i>Shake them up!</i>

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:31.940
Nom.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.460
Amazing...

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.930
<i>Here's my chance!</i>

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.440
<i>Sorry to have kept you waiting, Munemune.</i>

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:31.620
Two-all.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.660
Yes! They caught up!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.080
Beam, beam.

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.320
Are you okay?

00:20:56.930 --> 00:20:58.600
Now, let's go.

00:20:58.600 --> 00:20:59.290
Yeah!

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:01.930
Seven-eleven.

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:03.840
Game to Suzumegahara.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:05.780
Two games to one.

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.610
Eleven-nine!

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:10.290
Suzumegahara wins, three games to one!

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.250
Thank you very much.

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:20.210
Too bad.

00:21:21.350 --> 00:21:24.390
Looks like we need to
practice to death a lot more.

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:28.070
We won, huh?

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:31.510
If we'd lost, Agari would've
really let us have it.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:35.600
Let's go to Nationals.

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:38.170
Yeah, the two of us, together.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:40.740
Captain!

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:43.030
You did it, Senpai!

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.470
Nah, <i>all</i> of us, together.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Suzumegahara                     Mozuyama

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Tenka Hanabi                        Sasorida Sachiko

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Itsumo Hokuto                            Yuragi Yura

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Ushirode Kiruka
Munemune

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Kanenashi Mayuu
Hamu Kimiko

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Kamiya Agari                    Zashikiwarashi Zakuro

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:54.080
Tsumujikaze Koyori                   Futamaru Kururi

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.570
It's one-two now.

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:54.080
Go get 'em, Agari!

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.670
We're counting on you, Agari-senpai.

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:58.050
Win!

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.420
Agari-chan.

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:11.930
<i>Come what may,</i>

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:12.870
<i>victory is mine!</i>

00:23:43.860 --> 00:24:00.000
Preview

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:46.420
I-I won't quit!

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:48.790
I love the way you play
table tennis, Futamaru-san!

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:50.800
You'll miss out
on the most heart-racing moment.

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:52.420
The reason I play table tennis...

00:23:51.400 --> 00:23:55.200
I want to win and feel my heart race, too!

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:57.620
Most of all, I have to win for Kururi!
